Library: com.livecode.widget.piechart

Type: widget

Summary: A pie chart control. A pie chart displays a set of values and labels as sectors of a circular chart. The labels are displayed alongside the chart, and can be shown or hidden.

Name: sectorClicked

Type: message

Syntax: on sectorClicked pSectorNumber

Summary: Sent when a sector of the pie chart is clicked.

Parameters: 

pSectorNumber: The sector number of the clicked segment.

Description: The <sectorClicked > message is sent when a sector in the pie chart is clicked. The <pSectorNumber> parameter number of the sector which was clicked.


Name: sectorValues

Type: property

Syntax: get the sectorValues of <widget>

Syntax: set the sectorValues of <widget> to <pValueList>

Parameters: 

pValueList: A comma separated string of values.

Summary: The list of values to be displayed on the pie chart.

Description: Use the <sectorValues> property to set the values to be displayed in the pie chart.




Name: sectorLabels

Type: property

Syntax: get the sectorLabels of <widget>

Syntax: set the sectorLabels of <widget> to <pLabelList>

Parameters: 

pLabelList: A comma separated string of labels.

Summary: The list of labels associated with the pie chart sectors.

Description: Use the <sectorLabels> property to set the labels to be displayed in the pie chart.




Name: showLabels

Type: property

Syntax: get the showLabels of <widget>

Syntax: set the showLabels of <widget> to { true | false }

Summary: Whether the sector labels are shown or not.

Description: Use the <showLabels> property to control whether the sector labels are shown or not.




Name: sectorColors

Type: property

Syntax: get the sectorColors of <widget>

Syntax: set the sectorColors of <widget> to <pColorList>

Parameters: 

pColorList: A return-delimited list of colors, one for each sector, each as red,green,blue (0 to 255).

Summary: The colors of the pie chart sectors.

Description: Use the <sectorColors> property to set the colors of the sectors, in the order of <sectorValues>. When there are more sectors than colors, the colors start again from the first. Set it to empty to go back to the default colors.




Name: themedLabels

Type: property

Syntax: get the themedLabels of <widget>

Syntax: set the themedLabels of <widget> to { true | false }

Summary: Whether the sector labels follow the widget's text colour and font.

Description: When <themedLabels> is true, the sector labels are drawn in the widget's foreground colour and text font, so they stay readable in dark mode. When it is false, they are drawn in black in the default font, as pie charts were before version 1.0.1. A new pie chart starts with true; a pie chart saved before version 1.0.1 opens with false, so it looks as it did.
